response.text:
Looking at the screenshots, I found one real problem: the contact section, the hero card and the mobile call bar repeat the address and hours.

The contact section with the call-out variant already shows the address, hours and email. On mobile, the slice after it shows another "Obiščite nas" block with the address and directions link, and a second "Delovni čas" block. These come from the footer, so they are not a spec problem. The footer is fixed chrome and I leave it alone.

The hero card shows the address as its fact, which is intended for the card variant. The contact section is the only contact section on the homepage. The site has no contact page, so keeping it is allowed.

The CTA "Sprejemamo rezervacije za skupine do 60 oseb" and the contact intro "Rezervacije sprejemamo tudi za skupine do 60 oseb" say the same thing twice, directly one after the other. The fix is to shorten the contact intro so it no longer repeats the group claim. The contact title already says to call for a table reservation, so the intro can add something different.

The CTA copy says "Pišite nam", which fits the plural voice. The hero primary label "Rezervirajte mizo" calls, which is fine.

The team intro "Kuhamo in strežemo že tretja generacija." is grammatically off. It should read "že v tretji generaciji". I patch it.

```json
{
  "issues": [
    "The contact intro repeats the group reservation claim from the CTA directly above it.",
    "The team intro 'Kuhamo in strežemo že tretja generacija.' is ungrammatical Slovene."
  ],
  "patches": [
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/pages/0/sections/2/props/intro",
      "value": "Kuhamo in strežemo že v tretji generaciji."
    },
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/pages/0/sections/4/props/intro",
      "value": "Pokličite nas in mizo pripravimo za vas."
    }
  ]
}
```
